## SECTION 2 — REPOSITORY LAYER MODEL

2.1 Layer 0 — Governance Kernel

Owns:

* validation-state doctrine,
* claim escalation rules,
* authority routing,
* summary quarantine,
* unresolved-variable governance,
* contradiction handling rules,
* edit-impact chains,
* anti-duplication rules,
* terminology governance,
* canonical revision routing.

Does Not Own:

* subsystem mechanics,
* geometry,
* flotation behavior,
* processing logic,
* equipment design,
* operational throughput.

2.2 Layer 1 — Canonical Doctrine / Constraints

Owns:

* clean/dirty doctrine,
* inspectability doctrine,
* anti-hidden-failure principles,
* containment-first principles,
* prohibited geometries,
* maintenance-first doctrine,
* stable architectural boundaries.

Does Not Own:

* candidate results,
* mockup outcomes,
* measured behavior,
* operational claims.

2.3 Layer 2 — Candidate / Experimental Models

Owns:

* candidate architectures,
* Boat Prototype files,
* Build Notebooks,
* Geometry Control Files,
* exploratory interfaces,
* candidate layouts,
* mock geometry,
* candidate load paths.

Must Carry Explicit Status:

* candidate,
* mockup,
* measurement target,
* rejected,
* superseded,
* promoted.

Does Not Validate:

* payload capacity,
* reserve buoyancy,
* seaworthiness,
* operational readiness,
* containment performance,
* structural capability,
* ecological benefit,
* economic viability.

2.4 Layer 3 — Measurement / Reality Interrogation

Owns:

* mockups,
* float tests,
* ballast tests,
* strain observations,
* contradiction exposure,
* failure observations,
* measurement unlocks,
* controlled test logs,
* measurement records.

Only Layer 3 may initiate evidence-state promotion requests.

Measurement does not self-promote into validation.

2.5 Layer 4 — Interpretation / Editorial Layer

Owns:

* summaries,
* synthesis,
* onboarding material,
* explanatory narratives,
* editorial rewrites,
* cross-ledger observations,
* communication drafts.

Default Status:
[NON-CANONICAL]

Does Not Own:

* subsystem definitions,
* unresolved-variable status,
* validation-state authority,
* terminology governance,
* evidence-state promotion,
* canonical routing.

2.6 Layer 5 — Archive / Rejected Concepts

Owns:

* rejected geometries,
* abandoned assumptions,
* superseded concepts,
* contradiction history,
* rejected operational paths,
* failed approaches,
* archived reasoning.

Purpose:
Prevent cyclical rediscovery and preserve rejection rationale.

2.7 Layer 6 — Index / Retrieval Layer

Owns:

* concept-to-file routing,
* authority lookup,
* unresolved-variable lookup,
* terminology lookup,
* dependency lookup,
* ownership lookup,
* retrieval routing.

Purpose:
Answer:

* “what owns this?”
* “where does this belong?”
* “what depends on this?”
* “what validation state governs this?”

