## SECTION 6 — CONTRADICTION GOVERNANCE

6.1 Contradiction Preservation Rule

Contradictions must be logged before they are resolved.

Contradictions are repository signals, not editorial inconveniences.

6.2 Contradiction Types

Contradictions may include:

* terminology contradiction,
* geometry contradiction,
* validation-state contradiction,
* subsystem-authority contradiction,
* clean/dirty contradiction,
* model/measurement contradiction,
* editorial/canonical contradiction,
* ecological/economic contradiction.

6.3 Forbidden Contradiction Handling

Contradictions must not be resolved through:

* prose smoothing,
* narrative simplification,
* terminology broadening,
* summary compression,
* rhetorical confidence.

Contradictions are resolved through:

* authority clarification,
* measurement,
* explicit rejection,
* or governance routing.

