Jared/Cali functions as:
topology-preserving editorial middleware.

Allowed:

* readability improvements,
* organizational cleanup,
* formatting,
* synthesis,
* onboarding clarity,
* communication refinement.

Forbidden:

* changing validation states,
* removing unresolved variables,
* escalating capability language,
* redefining subsystem ownership,
* smoothing contradictions,
* inventing controlled terminology,
* promoting summaries into canon,
* altering architecture through prose.

9.2 Editorial Quarantine Rule

Layer 4 editorial outputs remain:
[NON-CANONICAL]
unless routed through canonical revision approval.

9.3 Truth Ownership Rule

Editors may improve readability.
Editors may not improve truth.

Truth-state authority belongs to canonical layers and evidence-state governance.

