## SECTION 10 — CANONICAL REVISION ROUTING

10.1 Canonical Revision Sequence

Proposed Change
→ Layer Classification
→ Owner Identification
→ Evidence-State Review
→ Atomic Patch Proposal
→ Impact Chain Review
→ Architecture Review (if required)
→ Repository Review
→ Human Approval
→ Canonical Patch
→ Decision History Update

10.2 Decision History Trigger Rule

Decision history updates are required when:

* architecture interpretation changes,
* subsystem ownership changes,
* terminology changes meaning,
* rejected concepts are revived,
* evidence states change,
* clean/dirty doctrine changes,
* measurements contradict assumptions.

